  "name": "Share OneDrive videos on LinkedIn, Shorts and Reels for Microsoft 365 teams with PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5a7ba804-75d3-4970-a74e-42210fa5f2f7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -668,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 792,
        "content": "## Share OneDrive videos on LinkedIn, Shorts and Reels\nDrop a video in a OneDrive folder and it goes out as a native LinkedIn video post, a YouTube Short, an Instagram Reel and a Facebook video, each with its own caption. For Microsoft 365 teams (marketing, HR, internal comms) who keep finished videos in OneDrive.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Microsoft OneDrive Trigger** watches a folder; **Only video files** skips everything else.\n2. **Describe the video** turns the file name into the idea for the captions and holds the networks and brand voice.\n3. PostWire hands out an upload slot and the file goes from OneDrive straight to it, so no public link is needed (a OneDrive share link opens a web page, not the file). Up to 50 MB.\n4. **Write the posts** returns a long LinkedIn post, a YouTube title and tags, and short captions for Reels and Facebook.\n5. **Publish the video** posts it everywhere. The OneDrive file ID is the idempotency key, so a retry never posts twice.\n6. If a network refuses, **Microsoft Outlook** emails the team what failed and how to fix it.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free account at postwire.io, connect your networks and copy your API key. In n8n add a **Header Auth** credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer pw_live_\u2026`) and select it in the four PostWire nodes.\n2. Connect Microsoft OneDrive and pick the folder in the trigger. Name each file after what the video says, for example quarterly-results-in-60-seconds.mp4.\n3. Connect Microsoft Outlook and set the team address.\n\n### Customize\nEdit the networks and brand voice in Describe the video, or swap Outlook for a Microsoft Teams message."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
